    33	## Reusable knowledge
    34	
    35	- A publication audit must search for actual `.tex`/`.pdf`, reconstruct every declared chunked artifact, compare declared size/SHA, and record unverifiable preflight claims separately. In the case audit, no manuscript existed; the ZIP and Base64 forms were truncated, so disposition was `scientific_closure: BLOCKED`, `evidence_integrity: INCOMPLETE`, `manuscript_state: NONE`, `technical_preflight: FAIL`, `human_signoff: PENDING`, `submission_route: UNDECIDED`. [Task 1]
    36	- `cd src && bash reproduce_local_dynamics.sh` emitted archived values but did not cold-replay because `rebuild_local_dynamics_result.json` was missing. Generated numerical output is not proof-replay evidence when declared archive/expected records are missing. [Task 1]
    37	- MathArc now rejects non-adjacent legacy claim pairs and duplicates; supports `\\matharcclaim{id}{revision}`; recursively collects `\\input`/`\\include` with cycle detection; blocks `.bib` without `.bbl`; and requires `INDEPENDENTLY_AUDITED` evidence plus nonempty human signoff before release-candidate readiness. Local publication tests passed 7/7, workflow policy and syntax compilation passed. [Task 2]
